counterfactuals.output:
1. A power conditioning system comprising:  
a fuel cell power source coupled to a direct-current link through a fuel-cell-side power converter;  
a battery power source coupled in parallel with the fuel cell power source at the direct-current link through a battery-side power converter;  
a control unit configured to control the fuel-cell-side power converter to supply power from the fuel cell power source to the direct-current link and to control the battery-side power converter to charge or discharge the battery power source;  
wherein the control unit is configured to synchronize an output voltage of the fuel-cell-side power converter and an output voltage of the battery-side power converter with a voltage of the direct-current link such that the fuel cell power source and the battery power source are operable in parallel on the direct-current link; and  
wherein the control unit is further configured to operate the battery-side power converter to suppress voltage or current ripple on the direct-current link by selectively absorbing ripple energy from, or injecting ripple-compensating energy into, the direct-current link.
